From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 12:58:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 41/62] verimark: temporarily log 0x99 no-match at WARN level
 for IT diagnose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

fp_info doesn't reach journalctl with the default fprintd config —
the diagnostic log added in the previous commit stayed invisible.
Bump to fp_warn so we can observe the firmware status word and
the first 8 payload bytes on the next verify-no-match attempt.

To revert once the IT match verdict is decoded.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index d2b8064..964d461 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -1191,10 +1191,11 @@ vfy_cb_match(GObject *src, GAsyncResult *res, gpointer ud)
         fp_info("verify: positive verdict on attempt %d (%zu bytes)",
                 ctx->attempt, payload_len);
     } else {
-        /* Logged at info level so the firmware status/payload shape is
-         * visible without a debug rebuild — useful for finding IT-
-         * specific match-on-chip codes (similar to enroll's 0x8006). */
-        fp_info("verify: attempt %d no-match (status 0x%04x, %zu bytes, "
+        /* Temporarily logged at WARN level so the firmware status/
+         * payload shape always reaches journalctl during IT diagnose
+         * (info/dbg get filtered out by default fprintd config). Once
+         * the IT match verdict is decoded, downgrade back to info. */
+        fp_warn("verify: attempt %d no-match (status 0x%04x, %zu bytes, "
                 "first 8 = %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x)",
                 ctx->attempt, status, payload_len,
                 payload && payload_len >= 1 ? payload[0] : 0,
